## Objective
- Adversarial read-only review of phase-096 (date/duration values in Redblue) at the redblue checkout, finding what is still wrong and emitting the exact `FINDINGS:` block plus mandatory `REVIEW VERDICT:` last line.

## Important Details
- Contract: READ-ONLY; only tools `read`, `grep`, `glob` available (no bash). Must cite `file:line` actually read. Every BLOCKER needs `VERIFIED:` marker; unverified BLOCKER is reported as MAJOR. Output severity exactly `BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR|STYLE`. If none: `FINDINGS: none`. Final line must be `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`, nothing after it.
- Gate is claimed green: `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (77 binaries, 2251 passed), `../rbops/verify.sh phase-096` pass.
- Phase adds `Value::Date(NaiveDateTime)` / `Value::Duration(TimeDelta)`, `time.date`, `time.datetime`, `time.duration`, six `add_*` calendar movers, date/duration properties, ordering/equality/arithmetic, plus uncommitted `time.from_unix`.
- chrono version in `Cargo.lock` is `0.4.45`; external registry source is not readable (external_directory denied), so chrono `TimeDelta::MIN`/`abs()` semantics cannot be directly confirmed.
- Committed change set includes a "resumed" round; uncommitted tracked changes add `time.from_unix`, shared `seconds_for_instant` helper, doc/test updates.
- Confirmed correct by reading: `BUILTIN_NAMES` count = 84 (lines 1163–1247), `MODULE_MEMBERS` count = 62 (time row line 128 has 14 members), doc-block anchors `SPEC.md:1410`, `SPEC.md:1439`, `SPEC.md:1522` all point at opening ```redblue fences, `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` new rows are substantive exact-output tests.

